*{{ill|Tsele Natsok Rangdröl|en|Tsele Natsok Rangdröl|qid=Q4503718|lt=Tsele Natsok Rangdröl|1=Tsele Natsok Rangdröl}} – ''Lamp of Mahāmudrā''{{sfnp|Rangdröl|2004}}
*{{ill|Kunkhyen Pema Karpo|en|Kunkhyen Pema Karpo|qid=Q464140|lt=Kunkhyen Pema Karpo|1=Kunkhyen Pema Karpo}} (1527–1592 CE) – ''Practice Guidelines of the Simultaneous School of Mahamudra'',{{sfnp|Roberts|2011}} ''The Oral transmission of the Six Cycles of Same Taste: Rolled into a ball [Path walking] instructions and "Mind Harvest", An instruction on the Five-Part Mahamudra'' 
*{{ill|Dagpo Tashi Namgyal|en|Dagpo Tashi Namgyal|qid=Q5208651|lt=Dagpo Tashi Namgyal|1=Dagpo Tashi Namgyal}} (16th century) – ''Clarifying the Natural State'' and ''Moonlight of Mahāmudrā''
*{{ill|Karma Chagme|en|Karma Chagme|qid=Q6372659|lt=Karma Chagme|1=Karma Chagme}} (1613–1678) – ''Meaningful to Behold''
